:: PART 1: Falling Action [part-start dark]
!Part One
!!Falling Action
----

The ''Redrockers'', those fickle schmucks, have decided your arc is over. They crumpled up the ''Draft'' and threw it in the bin like you weren't anything. But isn't that the point? No, really. Isn't that //your// point? Destined to be a footnote? There to support? There to usher things to a close. You're no ''Lead'', that's for sure, but there's nothing wrong with that. You're damn good at it.

What now? What now? What now? Move on. To your feet. Wake up, damn it.

<ul class="player-options">
    <li>[[You wake up.|Waking Up]]</li>
</ul>
:: Waking Up [dark]
Oh, goddamn it that was a mistake. Waking up was a mistake. Everything hurts. Every limb is throbbing. And you're dizzy. Wait, //are// you dizzy? Oh, no. No that's not it. You're lying on the ground. You're lying on your side.

You're lying on... What are the words for these sensations? Damn it. You're lying on something... //hot//. That's the word. And coarse. Gritty. Damn it. It's sand.

A pulsing roar, muffled and deep. Rumbling through the sand; through your throbbing bones. You're on a beach. But it's dark. 

<ul class="player-options">
    <li>[["Why is it dark?"]]</li>
</ul>

:: Why is it dark? [dark]

The darkness. The muffling. You've got a sack over your head. You should do something about that.

<ul class="player-options">
    <li>[[You do something about it.|The beach]]</li>
</ul>

:: The beach
''An unforgiving sun blinds you.''

You bring up your hand to shield your eyes. The hood slips from your other hand, then dissolves with a skittering on the sand. The hood's nanotech remains drift away on the breeze.

Your eyes adjust as you struggle to your knees. As you figured, you are on a pristine sandy ''beach''. A peaceful ocean, unnervingly clean and blue, stretches off to the horizon. It's a hack postcard vision of nature. Too perfect.

There is a ''crab'' here. "Hello," says the crab.

<ul class="player-options">
    <li>[[You look at the crab.]]</li>
</ul>

:: You look at the crab.
It is a crab. Friendly looking and pink, but a crab. It's small enough to fit on you hand, but not so small that you could easily crush it.

That's a messed up way of thinking about things. You meet a friendly crab and your first thought is ways to kill it?

<ul class="player-options">
    <li>[[What is wrong with you?]]</li>
</ul>

:: What is wrong with you?

The crab is looking you over, its eyestalks twitching expectantly.

<ul class="player-options">
    <li>[["\"What did you say?\""|INTRO: Benny]]</li>
</ul>